# Patch: 07_subbatch.diff
# Lever: L9, the inference sub-batch of predict_pdb.py: -subbatch N sets alphafold global_config.subbatch_size (the rows per chunk of every Attention module and every Transition, run through mapping.inference_subbatch; stock 4) to N before the model runner is built; the decision and its per-compiled-length record come from the model-opt tree's shared sub-batch policy (opt_core.jax_design.subbatch_policy) through the kit adapter af2ig_opt.subbatch and are written as `subbatch` timer records (alphafold/model/*.py untouched)
# Numerics class: TIER-2: changes numerics (other GEMM shapes and accumulation order per chunk; the same per-row math; not bitwise vs the stock body)
# Default: off; enabled only by predict_pdb.py -subbatch N (the af2ig_opt mode `fast` passes -subbatch 128, and `big` on its fast base)
# Applies to: nrbennet/dl_binder_design @ cafa3853ac94dceb1b908c8d9e6954d71749871a with 00-06 applied; apply with: patch -p1 < 07_subbatch.diff  (from the repository root)
# Licence: MIT, same as upstream dl_binder_design
#
